Z||000002||mrfixit58||07-07-2000||12:48 PM||||Check your local U-Pull-It yard. Every time I visit mine I see several 3.1 just sitting there. If you pull the crank yourself, it's $10. Rods are probably a buck. 2.8, 3.1, and 3.4s all use the same rod.<P>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||07-07-2000||01:22 PM||||3.1L and 3.4L use different rods than the 2.8L.<BR>2.8 to 3.1 is crank and rods differ<BR>3.1 to 3.4 bore is different.<BR>2.8 and 3.1 basically same block<BR>3.4 block has thicker cylinder walls with bigger bore.<P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-07-2000).]||||reg||4
